    "result_text": "The suite is green (BUILD SUCCESS). The project's only test class is `AcceptanceTest`, and it passes.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe spec requires that owners expose a `displayName` formatted exactly as `LastName, FirstName`. I implemented it with minimal structural impact by making two small changes to two files:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a `displayName` read-only string property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries the field.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added one `@Mapping` annotation to the existing `toOwnerDto` method that computes the value directly from the stored names:\n   ```java\n   @Mapping(target = \"displayName\", expression = \"java(owner.getLastName() + \\\", \\\" + owner.getFirstName())\")\n   ```\n\nBecause MapStruct routes single-owner, collection, and page mappings through `toOwnerDto`, the field is populated everywhere (including the `GET /api/owners/{id}` path the test reads back) with no changes to the entity, the endpoint YAML, or any function class. No method body grew and no large class was touched.",
